## Context
Successor of ticket 1237 (closed 2026-10-27 as overtaken, author's ruling). The gaze rewrite of
ticket 1225 (5cb969f5) took the adherence seat out of gaze; `tests/test_gaze_intent.py` now asserts
gaze names neither `adherence-seat` nor `adherence_verdict`. On origin/main e61b03dd nothing calls the
seat path: what remains is the machinery and the tests that pin it, plus one stale sentence
(`skills/verify-adherence/SKILL.md:52`, "`/gaze` passes it"). Hunt's self-gate runs verify-adherence
in its ordinary mode and never reaches `adherence_verdict.py`.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `scripts/adherence_verdict.py` and its tests are gone.
- [ ] `agents/adherence-seat.md` and `profiles/adherence-seat/` are gone, with their entries in
      `tests/test_agent_profiles.py` and `tests/test_profile_tool_grants.py`.
- [ ] verify-adherence drops the `semantic=caller` mode (argument hint, line 52 paragraph, § 3 caller
      section, the provisional-verdict line); the ordinary mode's text is unchanged.
- [ ] `git grep -n "semantic=caller\|adherence_verdict\|adherence-seat"` finds nothing outside
      `tickets/`, docs/discussions and memory; the gaze-intent negative assertion stays.
- [ ] Generated files regenerated (skills catalog, agent projections); the harness gate passes.

## Relevant files
scripts/adherence_verdict.py, tests/test_adherence_verdict.py, agents/adherence-seat.md,
profiles/adherence-seat/PROFILE.md, skills/verify-adherence/SKILL.md, tests/test_agent_profiles.py,
